!!id:"https://tson.io/test-suite/class2/schema/invalid/a-plain-supertype-does-not-compose-with-a-translations-record-expected.tn"
!!schema:"https://tson.io/test-suite/schemas/schema-sidecar.tn"
{
  spec: "[TSON-SCHEMA] §5.8"
  description: """
    A record's name type is set where it is declared, the kernel's default included: `address` says
    nothing, so its names are `field_name`'s, and `json_record`'s are `json_name`'s. A composition takes
    its supertypes' one name type and cannot change either, so `node` is refused at schema load -- even
    though `city` happens to be a `json_name` too, since a translation's type need not admit every
    identifier. `address => json_record & { city: text }` is the record to compose.
    """
  meta: "meta.tn"
  import: ["core.tn"]
  error: {
    category: resolver
  }
}
